WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Application data needs lower-layer delivery information.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
TCP identifies applications with ports and tracks bytes.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000
IP names endpoints A and B across networks.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.000
On LAN 1, Ethernet addresses the router as the local next hop.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.000
The switch forwards the frame; the router selects an outgoing route.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
New Ethernet framing uses router-to-B MACs. IP endpoints stay A and B.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.100
Ordinary routing without NAT. TTL also decreases.
